                    <description>&lt;p&gt;This issue was created by maloo for Andreas Dilger &amp;lt;adilger@dilger.ca&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This issue relates to the following test suite run: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/df2265f8-c35f-4596-9a0c-b53345f620b8" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/df2265f8-c35f-4596-9a0c-b53345f620b8&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;test_27cg failed with the following error:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;lfs setstripe: setstripe error for '/mnt/lustre/f27cg.sanity': Input/output error
 sanity test_27cg: @@@@@@ FAIL: setstripe failed 
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Test session details:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Interop&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Client&lt;br/&gt;
Lustre: 2.17.56.51&lt;br/&gt;
Branch: master&lt;br/&gt;
Build: &lt;a href="https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/130440" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/130440&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Kernel: 5.14.0-611.55.1.el9_7.x86_64&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Server&lt;br/&gt;
Lustre: 2.16.1.2&lt;br/&gt;
Branch: b2_16&lt;br/&gt;
Build: &lt;a href="https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-b2_16/6" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-b2_16/6&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Kernel: 5.14.0-427.31.1_lustre.el9.x86_64&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Has failed 8x in the past week of interop testing, which itself doesn't run very often.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The root cause needs to be investigated, since setstripe of a wide striped file itself shouldn't fail with a 2.16 server, so this seems like a real interop issue, and the test shouldn't just be skipped. &lt;/p&gt;







